# bootsheet.ps2 - the clicks the contact sheet is made of.
#
# ⭐ Time zero is PS2_SCRIPT_GATE: the moment `desk` prints DESK-READY, after
# its first full paint.  Everything before that on the sheet - the POST, the
# dialog, NitrOS-9 loading off the card - happens with NO INPUT AT ALL, which
# is the point: the machine gets itself to a desktop on its own.
#
# ⚠ Coordinates, origin and parking are files.ps2's, and for its reasons:
#
#   108 50    the "arm6309" disk icon on the desktop (desk.asm IcTab[0])
#   580 300   ⛔ THE PARK, and it is not decoration.  video3 draws the pointer
#             as a 16 x 16 SPRITE, so a pointer left on the window is sixteen
#             columns of whatever the sheet is about to show.
#
# ⭐ EVERY OPEN IS TWO CLICKS TEN SECONDS APART.  desk.asm has no double-click
# timer - a click selects and a click on the selection opens - deliberately,
# because the loop cannot measure time honestly.  So the sheet gets a tile of
# the icon SELECTED and a tile of the manager OPEN, which is a better picture
# of the interaction than a double-click would have been.
#
# ⛔ AND NOTHING IS CLICKED WHILE THE MANAGER IS REDRAWING.  boot-and-desktop.md
# §3.6: desk samples the button's level once a pass, and a pass that repaints
# twelve rows is 2.09 s, so a click inside one is not slow - it is gone.  Item
# 7 has the measured threshold: six clicks all arrive 2.2 s apart, three of six
# at 2.0 s.

origin 320 240
gap 120

# --- the card's icon: select it, then open it ------------------------------
at 2.000    move to 108 50
+0.700      click left      # selects the disk - and must not open it
+0.500      move to 580 300

at 12.000   move to 108 50
+0.700      click left      # ⭐ the file manager comes up on /SD0
+0.500      move to 580 300

# --- let the listing settle, then leave the picture alone ------------------
at 24.000   move to 580 300
